    "directions": [
      "Set up grill for indirect grilling and add two oak wood chunks to create smoke.",
      "Season the filets with kosher salt and freshly cracked black pepper.",
      "Once the grill reaches 250°F, introduce the steaks and monitor them with a wireless thermometer while preparing side dishes.",
      "Remove the steaks from the grill when they reach an internal temperature of 100 to 110°F and let them rest on a rack over a rimmed baking sheet.",
      "Remove the diffuser plate and put in the cast iron grill grates.",
      "Grill the steaks 3- to 4-minutes on each side, reaching 130 to 135°F for medium-rare, and 140 to 145°F for medium.",
      "Use an instant-read thermometer inserted sidewise into the thickest part of the steak to check doneness."
    ],
